  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Why Cookies Exist",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "State On A Stateless Wire",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "HTTP is stateless: every request independent, server remembers nothing",
            "Cookie = small key-value string the server asks browser to store",
            "Browser replays it on every later matching request",
            "Sent automatically — no JavaScript involved anywhere",
            "That automatic-ness is the root of CSRF"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "HTTP/1.1 200 OK",
            "Set-Cookie: sid=abc123   # server stores",
            "",
            "GET /account HTTP/1.1",
            "Cookie: sid=abc123       # browser replays"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "POST /login",
              "Set-Cookie",
              "browser jar",
              "Cookie: header",
              "server lookup"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Header Rules",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One `Set-Cookie` header per cookie — never comma-joined",
            "All matching cookies ride in ONE `Cookie` header",
            "`; ` separated: `Cookie: sid=abc; theme=dark`",
            "Values must be URL-encoded before sending",
            "Raw `;` `,` space or `=` in a value breaks parsing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Spec And Hard Limits"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Thing",
            "Value"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Born",
              "Netscape, 1994"
            ],
            [
              "Current spec",
              "RFC 6265bis"
            ],
            [
              "Per cookie",
              "~4096 bytes"
            ],
            [
              "Per domain",
              "~50 cookies"
            ],
            [
              "Whole jar",
              "~180 cookies"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Cookies Cost Bandwidth",
          "text": "They ride on EVERY matching request — images, CSS, fonts included. A 4KB cookie across 50 assets burns 200KB per page load."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Storage Rivals",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Store",
            "Auto-sent",
            "Server reads"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "cookie",
              "yes",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "`localStorage`",
              "no",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "`sessionStorage`",
              "no, per tab",
              "no"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Where To Put It",
          "text": "Cookie for anything the server needs. `localStorage` for client-only UI state. `sessionStorage` when it must die with the tab."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Not Encrypted By Default",
          "items": [
            "Stored plaintext on disk or in an OS keystore",
            "Profile folder access = cookie access",
            "Sign or encrypt anything you actually trust"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What People Store"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Session ID, auth token, CSRF token",
            "Locale, theme, A/B test bucket",
            "Analytics ID and consent record"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Misspelled Attribute Trap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Set-Cookie: sid=x; HttpOnley",
            "# typo: attribute dropped",
            "# stored anyway, JS can read it"
          ],
          "note": "no error in any console"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Set-Cookie Attribute Grammar",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Full Grammar",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Set-Cookie: name=value; Domain=x; Path=/;",
            "  Expires=...; Max-Age=...; Secure;",
            "  HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Partitioned"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`name=value` is the only required part",
            "Everything after a `;` is an attribute",
            "Order of attributes does not matter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Scope Attributes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Attribute",
            "Meaning",
            "Default"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Domain`",
              "which hosts get it",
              "host-only"
            ],
            [
              "`Path`",
              "URL prefix must match",
              "setting directory"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Path Default Bites",
          "text": "`Path` defaults to the directory of the setting request, not `/`. A response from `/app/login` quietly gets `Path=/app`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Lifetime Attributes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Expires=<HTTP-date>`",
              "absolute, GMT"
            ],
            [
              "`Max-Age=<seconds>`",
              "relative lifetime"
            ],
            [
              "`Max-Age=0` or negative",
              "delete now"
            ],
            [
              "neither present",
              "session cookie"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Expires=Wed, 09 Jun 2027 10:18:14 GMT",
            "Max-Age=86400   # wins if both present"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Session Cookie",
          "items": [
            "No `Expires`, no `Max-Age` = dies on browser close",
            "`Max-Age` beats `Expires` in all modern browsers",
            "'Restore tabs' can resurrect a session cookie"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Safety Attributes",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Secure` — only ever sent over HTTPS",
            "`HttpOnly` — hidden from `document.cookie`",
            "`SameSite` — cross-site send policy",
            "`Partitioned` (CHIPS) — one jar per embedding site"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Deleting Is Re-Setting",
          "text": "Same name, same `Domain`, same `Path`, plus `Max-Age=0`. Mismatch any of the three and you leave a zombie copy behind."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "res.cookie('sid', id, {",
            "  httpOnly: true, secure: true,",
            "  sameSite: 'lax', maxAge: 86400000",
            "})  // express helper"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Read The Raw Header",
          "text": "Frameworks parse `Cookie` into a map and silently drop duplicate names. When debugging, log the raw header string."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Silent Failures & Case Rules",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Silent Failure Modes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Attributes are NOT sent back — only `name=value` pairs",
            "Server cannot read a cookie's own `Path` or `Expires`",
            "Unknown attributes ignored: `HttpOnley` fails with zero errors",
            "Attribute names case-insensitive; cookie NAMES are not",
            "`sid` and `SID` are two different cookies"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Part",
            "Case-sensitive?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "attribute names",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "cookie names",
              "**yes**"
            ],
            [
              "cookie values",
              "yes"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Catch It Early",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Assert flags in a ==startup check==, not code review",
            "DevTools → Application → Cookies shows every flag",
            "`curl -i` prints the raw `Set-Cookie` line",
            "`document.cookie` hides `HttpOnly` cookies — that is expected"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Scoping By Domain",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Host-Only Vs Domain",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Set on",
            "Attribute",
            "Sent to"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`app.example.com`",
              "none",
              "`app.example.com` only"
            ],
            [
              "`app.example.com`",
              "`Domain=example.com`",
              "parent + ALL subdomains"
            ],
            [
              "`app.example.com`",
              "`Domain=.example.com`",
              "same — dot is legacy"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "example.com",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
