              },
              {
                "from": "b2",
                "to": "c2_0"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What The Browser Refuses"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "You cannot widen upward: `Domain=com` is rejected",
            "You cannot jump: `app.example.com` cannot set `other.com`",
            "No siblings: `a.example.com` cannot target `b.example.com`",
            "Only the shared parent is reachable",
            "Every rejection is silent — no error anywhere"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Public Suffix List",
          "items": [
            "Blocks cookies on registrable suffixes",
            "`.com`, `.co.uk`, `github.io` are all off-limits",
            "This is the 'supercookie' defence"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Subdomain Trap",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "XSS or takeover on `blog.example.com` reads a `Domain=` session",
            "Worse: it can also overwrite that cookie",
            "Cookie tossing: same name set on the parent shadows the real one",
            "Shadowed cookie enables session fixation",
            "Host-only is the safer default — widen only when forced"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Port Is Not Scope",
          "text": "`example.com:3000` and `example.com:8080` share one jar. Two dev servers on one host will happily stomp each other's login."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Scheme Is Half In",
          "text": "`Secure` cookies are HTTPS-only, but a non-`Secure` cookie set over HTTP is readable over HTTPS and vice versa. Cookies ignore same-origin policy."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Origin Vs Site & Cookie Tossing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Origin Is Not Site",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Origin = scheme + host + port",
            "Site = eTLD+1, the registrable domain",
            "`https://a.example.com` vs `http://b.example.com:8080`",
            "Different origins, same site — cookies see one thing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pair",
            "Origin",
            "Site"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`a.x.com` / `b.x.com`",
              "different",
              "**same**"
            ],
            [
              "`x.com:3000` / `x.com:8080`",
              "different",
              "**same**"
            ],
            [
              "`x.com` / `y.com`",
              "different",
              "different"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Practical Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each tenant or app gets its own host-only cookie",
            "Only SSO cookies deserve a parent `Domain`",
            "Audit which subdomains you actually trust"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Set Domain?",
            "rows": [
              [
                "q"
              ],
              [
                "a",
                "b"
              ],
              [
                "c"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "q": {
                "text": "subdomains need it?",
                "shape": "diamond"
              },
              "a": {
                "text": "host-only, no Domain",
                "shape": "box",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              "b": {
                "text": "Domain=parent",
                "shape": "box",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              "c": {
                "text": "audit every subdomain",
                "shape": "pill"
              }
            },
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "q",
                "to": "a",
                "label": "no"
              },
              {
                "from": "q",
                "to": "b",
                "label": "yes"
              },
              {
                "from": "b",
                "to": "c"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cookie Tossing Up Close",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "# served by evil.example.com",
            "Set-Cookie: sid=attacker;",
            "  Domain=example.com; Path=/app"
          ],
          "note": "longer Path is sent first"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Victim now sends `sid=attacker; sid=real` to `/app`",
            "Server reads the first — the ==attacker's== session",
            "Victim's actions land in the attacker's account"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "The Fix",
          "text": "Name the session `__Host-sid`. No `Domain` allowed, so no subdomain can plant a cookie with that name."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Server sends `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`",
            "`Allow-Origin` must be explicit — **never** `*`",
            "SameSite rules still apply on top"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Duplicate Names & Cross-Origin Fetch",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Duplicate Names"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One host-only `sid`, one `Domain=` `sid` — both sent",
            "Parsed map keeps one, often the wrong one",
            "Inspect the raw `Cookie` header, not the map"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cross-Origin fetch",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "fetch('https://api.x.com/me', {",
            "  credentials: 'include'",
            "})  // else no cookies"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "How can `blog.example.com` log me out of `app.example.com`?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Session was set with `Domain=example.com`",
            "Blog re-sets it with `Max-Age=0`",
            "Fix: host-only `__Host-` cookie on the app"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "Set-Cookie: sid=; Max-Age=0;",
            "  Domain=example.com; Path=/"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Path, Prefixes, Precedence",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How Path Matches",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "Path=/admin",
            "  /admin          # sent",
            "  /admin/users    # sent",
            "  /administrator  # NOT sent"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cookie path must be a prefix ending at a `/` boundary",
            "Or exactly equal to the request path",
            "Prefix-of-a-string alone is not enough"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Vanishing Cookie"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Default path = directory of the setting URL",
            "Response from `/app/login` becomes `Path=/app`",
            "Cookie then never reaches `/dashboard`",
            "Always set `Path=/` on session cookies"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Not A Security Boundary",
          "text": "Same-origin JavaScript reads cookies at any path through iframe tricks. Use `Path` for organisation, never for isolation."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Cookies, One Name",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same name at different paths = two separate cookies",
            "Browser sends both: `Cookie: sid=a; sid=b`",
            "Send order: longer `Path` first",
            "Equal paths tie-break by creation time, oldest first",
            "Most servers read only the first — shadowing is trivial"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Logged In As Someone Else",
          "text": "The server cannot tell which sent cookie came from which `Path`. This is a real source of wrong-user bugs, not a theoretical one."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Name Prefixes",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Prefix",
            "Browser demands"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "none",
              "nothing at all"
            ],
            [
              "`__Secure-`",
              "`Secure` + set over HTTPS"
            ],
            [
              "`__Host-`",
              "`Secure`, `Path=/`, no `Domain`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Set-Cookie: __Host-sid=abc; Secure;",
            "  Path=/; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Prefixes are enforced by the browser, not your server",
            "The name itself is the contract",
            "`__Host-` locks a cookie to the exact host",
            "No subdomain can overwrite it — best anti-tossing defence",
            "Use `__Host-session` for auth, always"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Same Cookie Or Not"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "When does a `Set-Cookie` update instead of duplicate?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Only when name + `Domain` + `Path` all match",
            "Any difference creates a second cookie",
            "That is how zombie sessions survive a logout"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Secure Flag & HSTS",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Secure: HTTPS Only",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Browser sends the cookie only over HTTPS",
            "`localhost` is exempted so dev still works",
            "Without it, one plain HTTP request leaks the session ID",
            "Hostile Wi-Fi plus sslstrip is a one-liner",
            "It restricts SENDING, not writing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Request to",
            "`Secure` cookie sent?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`https://site`",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "`http://site`",
              "**no**"
            ],
            [
              "`http://localhost`",
              "yes, dev exemption"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "What Secure Does Not Do",
          "items": [
            "Does not encrypt the cookie on disk",
            "Does not hide it from JavaScript",
            "Did not block HTTP overwrites on old browsers"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "HSTS Closes The Gap",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "Strict-Transport-Security:",
            "  max-age=31536000;",
            "  includeSubDomains; preload"
          ],
          "note": "preload covers the very first visit"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Why Both",
          "text": "`Secure` stops the cookie riding plain HTTP. ==HSTS== stops the browser making that plain HTTP request at all."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "HttpOnly & The Non-Negotiable Set",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The Overwrite Hole",
          "text": "Pre-RFC6265bis, plain HTTP could overwrite a `Secure` cookie even without reading it. Modern browsers block that — older ones did not."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "HttpOnly: Invisible To JS",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "document.cookie",
            "// 'theme=dark'   sid is absent",
            "// HttpOnly cookies never appear here"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`document.cookie` can neither read nor write it",
            "Does NOT stop XSS — stops token exfiltration",
            "Attacker with XSS still rides the session via same-origin `fetch`",
            "Still fully visible in DevTools and the network trace",
            "It raises attacker cost, it is not a wall"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
